777
01:02:48.031 --> 01:02:54.508
Bananas are a beloved fruit all around the
world, and the banana industry provides

778
01:02:54.508 --> 01:02:55.631
employment for

779
01:02:55.631 --> 01:03:01.391
thousands of people across tropical
regions of South America, the Caribbean,

780
01:03:01.391 --> 01:03:03.781
Southeast Asia and West Africa.

781
01:03:03.781 --> 01:03:09.602
If it is true that trading bananas is a
cornerstone in the economies of many

782
01:03:09.602 --> 01:03:10.402
countries,

783
01:03:10.402 --> 01:03:15.881
It is also true that there are complex
social problems related to this industry.

784
01:03:15.881 --> 01:03:21.532
During the period between the picking of a
banana and its purchase, the fruit can

785
01:03:21.532 --> 01:03:24.601
travel thousands of miles to get to a
store.

786
01:03:24.601 --> 01:03:28.351
However, its cost remains very low.

787
01:03:28.351 --> 01:03:34.701
How is it possible? It means that someone
in the supply chain is paying for it.

788
01:03:34.701 --> 01:03:39.801
In the case of bananas, the cost of
conventional, non-Fairtrade certified

789
01:03:39.801 --> 01:03:42.151
bananas falls on the farmers, who

790
01:03:42.151 --> 01:03:48.151
often live in conditions of poverty,
underpayment, health and safety risks,

791
01:03:48.151 --> 01:03:51.251
soil pollution and water shortages.

792
01:03:51.251 --> 01:03:57.287
And it also falls on the workers, whose
employment is precarious and whose wages

793
01:03:57.287 --> 01:03:58.087
are low.

794
01:03:58.087 --> 01:04:03.553
They also need to face the handling of
unhealthy and environmentally hazardous

795
01:04:03.553 --> 01:04:04.354
chemicals.

796
01:04:04.354 --> 01:04:10.273
Nella slide successiva andiamo avanti.
Fairtrade works with banana farmers,

797
01:04:10.273 --> 01:04:11.073
workers

798
01:04:11.073 --> 01:04:15.331
and with the banana trade to create more
value for the producers,

799
01:04:15.331 --> 01:04:20.971
And ensure that workers get a decent pay
for the hard work that is necessary to

800
01:04:20.971 --> 01:04:22.061
grow this crop.

801
01:04:22.061 --> 01:04:27.171
The first Fairtrade bananas were sold in
the Netherlands in 1996.

802
01:04:27.171 --> 01:04:33.541
In 2023, Fairtrade announced higher
minimum prices for bananas,

803
01:04:33.541 --> 01:04:39.241
as a way to counterbalance the impact of
skyrocketing production and living costs.

804
01:04:39.241 --> 01:04:46.184
People from Fairtrade asked retailers and
traders to continue to support Fairtrade

805
01:04:46.184 --> 01:04:46.984
bananas,

806
01:04:46.984 --> 01:04:48.911
although prices were higher.

807
01:04:48.911 --> 01:04:55.616
Quindi un testo dove trovate delle
